From ccdf046853f4fb9fae9115f9e4ebaaf65c609681 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kryxzort <virajslko@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:52:06 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] audio: host audio output driver
 (wp_config_set_audio_output)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

An embedder that owns audio output (its own mixer, a PipeWire stream with
dB gains and ramps) had no way to take LWE's sound: every context opened an
SDL audio device at creation, even with audio disabled, and the only
controls were a coarse linear 0..128 volume and a mute check that pauses.

wp_config_set_audio_output (config, {sample_rate, channels}) makes contexts
created from that configuration use a new HostAudioDriver instead of the SDL
one: no SDL audio subsystem, no device. The host pulls the unity-gain mix of
every stream as F32 interleaved PCM with wp_context_audio_pull, from its
own audio thread. A pull never waits for decoding (an empty packet queue is
silence for that pull and wakes the read thread), so it is safe from a
real-time callback. Not pulling pauses the sound where it is; the frames a
host pulls per second of its own clock set the playback rate, so it can
also change speed through a time-stretch stage of its own.

wp_context_audio_stream_count and wp_context_audio_driver_name ("host" |
"sdl") report what a context plays. Without an output nothing changes:
SDL stays the default. The driver's stream list is mutex-guarded
(add/remove come from the render thread, pulls from the host's) and frees
its buffers on removal.

Origin: ours
Why: lp-player owns scene audio as a dB-gained PipeWire stream (ramps, equal-power crossfades, speed with pitch correction); the SDL device could only be controlled from outside (docs/player/spikes/lwe-core.md §4.1)
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
